column4:
You can add another IF...THEN...ELSE in the timer (double click the timer, or you can say in event Timer.OnTimer).
Let's said by default (interval is 1000), you have a set of instruction in Timer. And after the interval is changed to 3000, you want the timer "do" something else.
Well just do like this
Timer.OnTimer
  IF (Timer.Interval = 1000) THEN
   {your instruction here}
  ELSE IF (Timer.Interval = 3000) THEN
   {your instruction here}
  ELSE
   {your instruction here};
end;
Like that. That way, the timer will do something different each time you change the interval. You can add more (ELSE IF... THEN) if you want more instruction for different intervals.

